    {"channel": "CDEC", "ts": "1700000000.000001", "user": "UERIN",
     "text": "We need to pick a date-picker library for the new booking flow. Options on the table: react-aria, react-datepicker, and rolling our own."},
    {"channel": "CDEC", "ts": "1700000060.000002", "user": "UDANA",
     "text": "react-datepicker is the most popular but its keyboard accessibility is weak and it drags in moment.js", "thread_ts": "1700000000.000001"},
    {"channel": "CDEC", "ts": "1700000120.000003", "user": "UFRANK",
     "text": "rolling our own is too much maintenance burden for the team right now", "thread_ts": "1700000000.000001"},
    {"channel": "CDEC", "ts": "1700000180.000004", "user": "UERIN",
     "text": "react-aria (from Adobe) gives us accessible, unstyled primitives — WCAG behavior out of the box and no heavy dependencies. I think that's the move.", "thread_ts": "1700000000.000001"},
    {"channel": "CDEC", "ts": "1700000240.000005", "user": "UFRANK",
     "text": "agreed, react-aria it is. can someone write up a short summary and pin it so newcomers can find what we landed on?", "thread_ts": "1700000000.000001"},
    {"channel": "CGEN", "ts": "1700000300.000006", "user": "UDANA",
     "text": "the booking flow redesign is moving along, picking the component libs this week"}
  ]
}
